I dropped out of college, did four years of high school online, and sacrificed my entire
social life just to build a business.
And if I could go back in time, I would not do this all over again.
I significantly underestimated how long it would take.
When you first start, the opportunities seem endless, which they are.
That also makes you convince yourself that you could shortcut the path and get to success
in a very short amount of time.
And when you believe that to be true, even if you're winning on paper, everything just
feels miserable.
But the reason why I love what I do now is because I've just extended my time horizon.
Instead of thinking months or even years ahead, I now try to think in three, five,
ten-year timelines.
So if I could go back in time and do this again, I only would if I could tell myself that
it would take way longer than expected.
